+# Company Vacation Policy
+
+**Effective Date:** January 1, 2024
+**Last Updated:** November 24, 2024
+**Department:** Human Resources
+
+## Overview
+
+This document outlines the vacation and paid time off (PTO) policy for all full-time employees. Our goal is to support work-life balance while maintaining operational efficiency.
+
+## Eligibility
+
+All full-time employees are eligible for PTO benefits starting from their first day of employment. Part-time employees working 20+ hours per week receive prorated benefits.
+
+## PTO Allowance
+
+### Based on Years of Service
+
+| Tenure | Annual PTO Days |
+|--------|-----------------|
+| 0-2 years | 15 days |
+| 2-5 years | 20 days |
+| 5-10 years | 25 days |
+| 10+ years | 30 days |
+
+### Accrual Rate
+
+PTO accrues on a monthly basis at the following rates:
+- **0-2 years:** 1.25 days per month
+- **2-5 years:** 1.67 days per month
+- **5-10 years:** 2.08 days per month
+- **10+ years:** 2.5 days per month
+
+## Requesting Time Off
+
+### Process
+
+1. Submit PTO request through the HR portal
+2. Manager approval required within 5 business days
+3. Requests should be submitted:
+   - 2 weeks in advance for 1-3 days
+   - 4 weeks in advance for 4+ days
+   - 8 weeks in advance for 2+ weeks
+
+### Blackout Periods
+
+The following periods have limited PTO availability:
+- December 15 - January 5 (Holiday season)
+- Quarter-end close periods (last week of March, June, September, December)
+
+During blackout periods, manager and director approval is required.
+
+## Carryover Policy
+
+- Maximum of **5 days** may be carried over to the next calendar year
+- Carried over days must be used by March 31
+- Days beyond the carryover limit are forfeited (use it or lose it)
+
+## Holidays
+
+In addition to PTO, employees receive the following paid holidays:
+- New Year's Day
+- Martin Luther King Jr. Day
+- Presidents' Day
+- Memorial Day
+- Independence Day
+- Labor Day
+- Thanksgiving Day
+- Day after Thanksgiving
+- Christmas Eve
+- Christmas Day
+
+## Special Circumstances
+
+### Sick Leave
+- Separate from PTO
+- 10 days per year
+- Does not carry over
+
+### Bereavement Leave
+- 5 days for immediate family
+- 3 days for extended family
+
+### Jury Duty
+- Paid leave for duration of service
+- Must provide documentation
+
+## Contact
+
+For questions about this policy, contact:
+- **HR Department:** hr@company.com
+- **HR Portal:** https://hr.company.internal
+- **Phone:** (555) 123-4567
+
+---
+
+*This policy is subject to change. Employees will be notified of any updates via email.*
