+# Engineering Deployment Guide
+
+**Version:** 2.1.0
+**Last Updated:** November 2024
+**Owner:** Platform Engineering Team
+
+## Overview
+
+This guide covers the standard deployment process for production applications. All deployments must follow these procedures to ensure system stability and compliance.
+
+## Prerequisites
+
+Before deploying, ensure:
+
+- [ ] All tests pass in CI/CD pipeline
+- [ ] Code review approved by 2+ engineers
+- [ ] Security scan completed (no critical/high vulnerabilities)
+- [ ] Database migrations reviewed by DBA
+- [ ] Change request approved (for production)
+- [ ] Rollback plan documented
+
+## Environments
+
+| Environment | Purpose | Deployment |
+|-------------|---------|------------|
+| Development | Feature development | Automatic on PR |
+| Staging | Integration testing | Automatic on merge to main |
+| Production | Live traffic | Manual approval required |
+
+## Deployment Process
+
+### 1. Pre-Deployment Checklist
+
+```bash
+# Verify current state
+git status
+git log --oneline -5
+
+# Ensure on correct branch
+git checkout main
+git pull origin main
+
+# Run local verification
+npm test
+npm run build
+```
+
+### 2. Create Release
+
+```bash
+# Create release tag
+git tag -a v1.2.3 -m "Release v1.2.3: Feature description"
+git push origin v1.2.3
+
+# Or use release script
+./scripts/create-release.sh v1.2.3
+```
+
+### 3. Deploy to Staging
+
+Staging deploys automatically when:
+- A new tag is pushed matching pattern `v*.*.*`
+- CI/CD pipeline passes
+
+Monitor staging deployment:
+```bash
+# Check deployment status
+kubectl get deployments -n staging
+
+# View logs
+kubectl logs -f deployment/app -n staging
+
+# Verify health
+curl https://staging.company.com/health
+```
+
+### 4. Production Deployment
+
+Production requires manual approval:
+
+1. Open GitHub Actions workflow
+2. Select "Deploy to Production" workflow
+3. Click "Run workflow"
+4. Enter release version
+5. Wait for approval from platform team
+
+### 5. Post-Deployment Verification
+
+```bash
+# Check deployment status
+kubectl get deployments -n production
+
+# Verify health endpoints
+curl https://api.company.com/health
+curl https://api.company.com/ready
+
+# Check metrics dashboard
+open https://grafana.company.internal/d/production-overview
+```
+
+## Rollback Procedure
+
+If issues are detected:
+
+### Immediate Rollback (< 5 min)
+
+```bash
+# Rollback to previous deployment
+kubectl rollout undo deployment/app -n production
+
+# Verify rollback
+kubectl rollout status deployment/app -n production
+```
+
+### Manual Rollback
+
+```bash
+# Deploy specific version
+kubectl set image deployment/app app=registry.company.com/app:v1.2.2
+
+# Or use Helm
+helm rollback app 42 -n production
+```
+
+## Database Migrations
+
+### Forward Migrations
+
+```bash
+# Run migrations
+npm run migrate:up
+
+# Verify migration status
+npm run migrate:status
+```
+
+### Rollback Migrations
+
+```bash
+# Rollback last migration
+npm run migrate:down
+
+# Rollback to specific version
+npm run migrate:to 20241101_create_users
+```
+
+**Important:** Database rollbacks may cause data loss. Always backup before migration.
+
+## Monitoring & Alerts
+
+### Key Metrics to Watch
+
+- Error rate (should be < 0.1%)
+- P99 latency (should be < 500ms)
+- CPU/Memory utilization (should be < 80%)
+- Active connections
+- Queue depth
+
+### Alert Escalation
+
+| Severity | Response Time | Escalation |
+|----------|--------------|------------|
+| Critical | 5 min | On-call + Manager |
+| High | 30 min | On-call |
+| Medium | 4 hours | Next business day |
+| Low | 24 hours | Sprint planning |
+
+## Contacts
+
+- **On-Call:** #platform-oncall (Slack)
+- **Platform Team:** platform@company.com
+- **Emergency:** (555) 911-HELP
+
+## Appendix
+
+### Common Issues
+
+**Deployment stuck in pending:**
+```bash
+kubectl describe deployment/app -n production
+# Check for resource constraints or image pull issues
+```
+
+**Health check failing:**
+```bash
+kubectl exec -it deployment/app -- curl localhost:8080/health
+# Verify application is starting correctly
+```
+
+**Database connection issues:**
+```bash
+# Check connection pool
+kubectl exec -it deployment/app -- npm run db:check
+```
+
+---
+
+*For detailed troubleshooting, see the [Troubleshooting Guide](./troubleshooting.md)*
